{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>Who says.</b> And 'who says to Jerusalem, it shall be built' — and behold, this is complete proof that Jerusalem was built in the days of Cyrus. And he hinted at 'you shall be founded' regarding the House of HaShem, which he commanded to be built. And when the hands of Zerubbabel laid it, Cyrus commanded that it not be built. And thus it has been established that Daniel did not err in his calculation, as I explained in its place."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:03.677248917Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}